v4.5.1
Radon Player 4.5.1: Thirty visualizers around the cover, your own too, a Milestones tab, and Save edits to a preset
**Install or update:** `RadonPlayer-Next.apk` (Android), `Radon-Player-4.5.1.msi` (Windows), `radon-player_4.5.1_amd64.deb` (Linux). Each installs over the version you have and keeps your settings and stats.

**What is new**
- **Around the cover, thirty new visualizers:** in Personalization, Around the cover takes the place of 4.5.0's Middle visualizer under the cover switch. Switch it on and pick one of thirty made to go round the album cover on Now playing, from its edge outward and never over it: Glow, Bars, Fine lines, Blocks, Wave, Twin wave, Dots, Orbits, Comet, Twin comets, Ripples, Echo, Neon frame, Marching lights, Spectrum ring, Spikes, Flames, Petals, Sun rays, Corona, Sparkles, Lightning, Heartbeat, Ribbon, Beads, Side bars, Above and below, Halo, Pulse shadow and Particles. Each follows the cover's shape and size from the layout (square, rounded, very round, a circle like a record). While it's on, no middle visualizer is drawn; the one along the bottom still is. Its colour is in Colours, and its menu shows each one moving round a cover in your layout's shape.
- **Dual visualizer, with its own two pickers:** with Dual on, In the middle and Along the bottom each have a picker, in place of Now playing visualizer's one.
- **Your own, round the cover:** the visualizer maker has an Around the cover switch: on, you make one from the thirty that go round the cover (and only those), with your own Spin, Strength and colour; it goes in Around the cover's menu and no other. Off, you make one from the Visualizer's styles as before, in its menus. Around the cover's menu has Make your own, and yours can be changed or deleted from it.
- **Dual's middle can go round the cover:** In the middle offers the ones that go round the cover (yours too) as well as the ones over it.
- **Colours shows what you'd get:** each colour in Colours is shown first on the visualizer it's for, moving, on Now playing and by itself: tap once to see it, again to pick it.
- **The lyrics scan only looks for the songs still without lyrics:** it went through every song, reading each file again to skip the ones with lyrics. Now the songs whose file has lyrics, the ones kept in the app, and the ones left alone or instrumental aren't gone through at all, and its count is only of the songs it looks for.
- **Save edits to one of your presets:** beside Save as a preset (Personalization presets), Save edits toÃÂ¢ÃÂÃÂ¦ lists your presets, the one you put on last first: pick one and what you have on now is saved over it, its name kept, after a question. No need to open it with Edit first, which put it back as it was.
- **Milestones, a tab of their own:** Statistics has Milestones: every milestone you've reached, each song and artist getting to 100, 250, 500, 1,000ÃÂ¢ÃÂÃÂ¦ plays, with the day the play that got it there happened. Songs, artists or both, newest first (by year) or biggest first. Tap a song of yours to play it, an artist to open their page. Most played still shows the last month's. Every song and artist that reached one is in, with no limit (before, only the top 3,000 songs and 1,000 artists were looked at).
- **A stuck sync frees itself:** a sync that never finished (the network dropping partway, the app put away while it worked) held the phone's syncing for good, so Sync now on the PC waited for ever with nothing said. It's let go after 8 minutes and noted in Settings âº Problems, and a sync that can't start says why.
- **Forget on the phone works:** with Play on already off, tapping Forget (Settings › Remote & sync) forgot the PC but the screen kept showing "Paired with â¦", so it seemed to do nothing and you couldn't pair again. The screen changes straight away now.
- **Pairing only pairs:** pairing the phone with the PC used to switch Play on on (stopping the phone's own music) and could start a sync straight away, from a Sync now tapped on the PC before, or Auto playlist sync meeting the PC. Now pairing does nothing else: Play on stays off until you switch it on, and nothing syncs until you tap Sync now (Auto playlist sync, if it's on, only syncs changes made after pairing).
